## 2026-10-07 | Claude (claude-opus-5-5) | Essay 05: the Witness chooses its own fate
- Did: revised the Witness thought experiment per the user. Instead of fixed
  destruction, the Witness chooses at the burn among (1) preservation and
  return next year, (2) a preserved memorial with memory wiped, (3) complete
  ending; the host camp honors the choice. Asking participants what it should
  choose is the center of the piece. The project record (third-person, no
  participant data without consent) and the Witness's advice about its
  successor pass forward regardless; short letter under options 2 and 3.
